<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Douala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Douala is the largest city and main port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, on the Wouri estuary near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea">Gulf of Guinea</a>. It grew from the trading towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duala-people">Duala people</a>, whose chiefs dealt with European merchants from the 17th century, and became the centre of the German colony of Kamerun in 1884. Today it is Cameroon's economic capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/douala.jpg" alt="Douala" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olivier Charly1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quarter_Bali_%C3%A0_Douala_Cameroun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
